\bibitem [{NoH()}]{NoHairCaveat}%
  \BibitemOpen
  \href@noop {} {}\bibinfo {note} {A realistic theory of gravity should be
  compatible with observed black-hole phenomenology, as supported by
  gravitational-wave detections \cite{Abbott2016.PRL.116.061102} and Event
  Horizon Telescope observations \cite{Akiyama2019.ApJL.875.L1}. Nevertheless,
  the absence of identified black-hole solutions beyond Schwarzschild and the
  scarcity of asymptotically flat branches in Sec.~\ref{sec:V} should not
  simply be taken as negative results. The key question is not only which
  static exact solutions exist, but which local gravitational configurations
  are dynamically realized in the real Universe. In particular, the final
  exterior state may still be the Schwarzschild branch with $S_\mu=0$.
  Gravitational collapse and stability analyses are needed to answer this
  question.}\BibitemShut {Stop}%
