  represents a fine-tuned initial state \cite {Ellis2004.CQG.21.223}. In this
  sense, the horizon problem is not solved dynamically, but shifted to the
  assumption of a fine-tuned \protect \textit {homogeneous} initial state. By
  contrast, ESHU corresponds to a saddle-type attractor and can emerge from an
  ordinary expanding epoch.}\BibitemShut {Stop}%
