  behaviour of Eq.~(\ref{eq:3.25}) along its centre manifold, i.e., the
  $z_1$-axis (see discussions below Eq.~(\ref{eq:3.26})). These two dynamical
  systems impose opposite stability requirements along the centre manifold. One
  requires the centre-manifold direction to be repelling, whereas the other
  requires it to be attracting. This distinction makes the vanishing flow fatal
  for Eq.~(\ref{eq:3.29}), but not for Eq.~(\ref{eq:3.25}).}\BibitemShut
