  follows from Eq.~(\ref {eq:A.05}), and expand $g_c(u_h,u_c)$ near the origin.
  The first nonzero terms are quadratic, of the form $u_h^2$, $u_h u_c$, and
  $u_c^2$. Since the centre-manifold expansion implies $u_h\propto u_c^2$ near
  the origin, the terms involving $u_h$ are higher order. Therefore, $\phi
  (u_c)$ does not enter the leading term of $g_c(\phi (u_c),u_c)$.}\BibitemShut
